    h3 "Sizes #" @42,2404,669,19
    text The button comes in 4 different sizes: @42,2435,669,20
    text small @42,2467,669,21
    text normal @42,2500,669,20
    text medium @42,2532,669,20
    text large @42,2564,669,20
    text While the default size is the normal one, the is-normal modifier exists in case you need to reset the button to its normal size. @42,2596,669,41
    text Example @42,2649,669,20
    row @42,2681,669,37
      button Small @42,2681,68,37
      button Default @122,2681,80,37
      button Normal @214,2681,80,37
      button Medium @306,2681,85,37
      button Large @403,2681,69,37
    text HTML @42,2730,669,20
    text <button class="button is-small">Small</button> <button class="button">Default</button> <button class="button is-normal">Normal</button> <button class="button is-medium">Medium</button> <button class="button is-large">Large</button> @42,2762,669,61
    button Copy danger @42,2835,669,36
    text You can change the size of multiple buttons at once by wrapping them in a buttons parent, and applying one of 3 modifiers: @42,2883,669,41
    text buttons are-small @42,2936,669,20
    text buttons are-medium @42,2968,669,20
    text buttons are-large @42,3000,669,21
    text Example @42,3033,669,20
    row @42,3065,669,36
      button All @42,3065,48,36
      button Medium @102,3065,85,36
      button Size @199,3065,59,36
    text HTML @42,3113,669,21
    text <div class="buttons are-medium"> <button class="button">All</button> <button class="button">Medium</button> <button class="button">Size</button> </div> @42,3146,669,40
    button Copy danger @42,3198,669,36
    text You can change the size of only a subset of buttons by simply applying a modifier class to them. For example, if you want all buttons to be small but still have one in its normal size, simply do the following: @42,3246,669,61
    text Example @42,3319,669,21
    row @42,3352,669,36
